-- title:
--   Principal regular stalk ideal descends to a generator in I(U)
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and $I$ an element of `X.IdealSheafData`, so that for each affine open $U$ of $X$ one has an ideal `I.ideal U` of the ring of sections $\Gamma(X, U)$. Fix an affine open $U$ of $X$, a point $x$ of $X$ with $x \in U$, and an element $\pi$ of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$. Assume that the image of the ideal `I.ideal U` under the germ map $\Gamma(X, U) \to \mathcal{O}_{X,x}$ at $x$ is the principal ideal generated by $\pi$, and that $\pi$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$. Write $\mathfrak p \subset \Gamma(X, U)$ for the prime ideal of $\Gamma(X, U)$ corresponding to $x$ under the affineness of $U$ (`U.2.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩`). The conclusion is the existence of a section $g \in \Gamma(X, U)$ such that $g$ lies in `I.ideal U`, the image of `I.ideal U` in the localisation $\Gamma(X, U)_{\mathfrak p}$ is the ideal generated by the image of $g$, and the image of $g$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\Gamma(X, U)_{\mathfrak p}$.
--
--   This converts a stalkwise statement — the ideal sheaf is locally principal at $x$ with regular generator — into the same statement over the localisation $\Gamma(X,U)_{\mathfrak p}$, with the further information that the generator may be taken to be the image of an honest section belonging to $I(U)$. It is used in the analysis of the ideal sheaf cutting out a point on the two-chart model of $X_1(p)$, where the local invertibility of that ideal sheaf is checked stalk by stalk.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_exists_mem_ideal_and_map_eq_span_singleton_and_mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_map_germ_eq_span_singleton.lean

